From 8e4e50b86bbeb3de432a3092249d6c172fa1ee8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@inscope-labs.dev>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:00:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shell): finalize Standard-tier manifest with real
 SHA-256 hashes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the obsolete first-draft standard.json (fallbackSystemPath-
based, no sha256, mismatched applet set) with the real Standard-delta
manifest: 22 BusyBox applets sourced from the same 1.36.1 pin as Base,
sharing one libbusybox_standard.so per ABI via sharedBinaries[], hashes
verified from the build-busybox-standard-delta workflow artifacts
(all 3 ABIs green after CI fix attempt 3, 4b5feb3).

Schema matches base.json exactly (sharedBinaries[] + per-ABI sha256
object + binaries[] referencing sharedBinary id, no fallbackSystemPath).

required:false throughout — Standard is an optional DFM per the
RTX-100 contract, unlike Base's required:true core applets.

Binary placement (shell_standard/src/main/jniLibs/<abi>/) to follow
in a separate commit once the real .so files are copied in, same
sequencing as Base's bf0df46 -> b7c63b8.
